{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Her Nazirites were purer than snow, whiter than milk</b> — <b>משלג ומחלב</b> is doubled, and likewise <b>ספיר</b> is like <b>פנינים</b>. And so its accent [te'amim]: the mem of <b>מפנינים</b> draws itself and what follows after it, like the mem of <b>מאל אביך</b> (Genesis 49:25), as though it were detached from <b>ספיר</b>. And <b>לבנת</b> (Exodus 24:10) is like <b>לבנה</b>, and the proof is \"כמעשד\" [\"like the work of\"], and in another place <b>אבן</b> (Ezekiel 1:26)."], :book :lamentations, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The accent notation passage is compressed; rendered the claim about the mem of מפנינים drawing itself and what follows it hyper-literally. The quotation כמעשד preserved exactly as in source (defective spelling of כמעשה); the intended full phrase from Exodus 24:10 is כמעשה לבנת הספיר."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Lamentations -- Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%94"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:12.012416713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}